    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_cta",
      "label": "Show Button",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_text",
      "label": "Button Text",
      "default": "Shop Retinol Series"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "Button Link"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content: Definition"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "definition_title",
      "label": "Definition Heading",
      "default": "What Is Retinol?"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "definition_text",
      "label": "Definition Text",
      "default": "<p>Retinol is a form of Vitamin A, a nutrient essential for skin health. Unlike exfoliants that work on the surface, Retinol operates at a cellular level. It penetrates deep into the dermis to neutralize free radicals and boost the production of elastin and collagen, creating a 'plumping' effect that reduces the appearance of fine lines, wrinkles, and enlarged pores.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content: Benefits"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefits_title",
      "label": "Benefits Heading",
      "default": "Visible Results"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content: Ritual"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ritual_title",
      "label": "Ritual Heading",
      "default": "Usage Protocol"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "ritual_text",
      "label": "Ritual Text",
      "default": "<p>Apply a pea-sized amount to clean, dry skin only at night. If you are new to Retinol, start by using it twice a week to allow your skin to adjust, then gradually increase frequency. It is vital to use a broad-spectrum sunscreen every morning, as Retinol can increase skin sensitivity to the sun.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "alert_text",
      "label": "Alert/Warning Text",
      "default": "Note: Do not use simultaneously with Vitamin C or AHAs."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "benefit",
      "name": "Benefit Card",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "benefit_title",
          "label": "Benefit Title",
          "default": "Benefit Name"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "benefit_desc",
          "label": "Description",
          "default": "Description of the benefit."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
